<h2>Division Game Day</h2>
<p><strong>Original 2021 learning goal:</strong> Practice dividing whole numbers within 100.</p>
<p>Warm-up Number Talk: mentally divide 48 by 2, 3, 4 and 6, obtaining 24, 16, 12 and 8. Discuss the related multiplication facts for 48.</p>
<h3>Race to 1</h3><p>Play with the original source starter numbers 12, 16, 18, 24, reroll divisor five, use recorded quotients or fresh starters, and finish at quotient 1. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<h3>Compare, Division</h3><p>Use two-player comparison with teacher-approved division cards and explain winning quotient comparisons. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<p>Original public source lesson: <a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-8/lesson-11/lesson.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2021 teacher material</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Original-source limitation:</strong> The original Race to 1 physical table and Compare division card masters remain unverified. Publisher-gated Cool-down is not claimed.</p></section>
